LCD L37044 — Repeat Sleep Studies

Repeat polysomnography is covered only when ONE of the following medical necessity criteria is documented:
(a) Failure of prior treatment with documented clinical change (worsening daytime symptoms, weight gain >10%, new comorbidity);
(b) Need to retitrate CPAP/BiPAP after >12 months on therapy;
(c) New onset of central sleep apnea on prior treatment;
(d) Treatment failure with documented inadequate adherence or persistent symptoms despite >=4 hours nightly use.

Repeat studies for patient request, second opinion, or without intervening treatment trial are NOT covered.

LCD L38419 — Whole Exome and Whole Genome Sequencing

Whole exome sequencing (WES) is covered for patients with suspected genetic disease when ALL prerequisites are met:
1. Prior single-gene or targeted panel testing has been performed and is non-diagnostic, OR the suspected condition is too genetically heterogeneous for targeted testing;
2. Genetic counseling has been provided and documented before testing, including informed consent for incidental findings;
3. Results will inform clinical management or reproductive decision-making.

Single negative gene test alone does not satisfy the tiered-testing requirement; documented targeted panel testing or appropriate justification for skipping is required before WES is covered.

LCD L34522 / NCD 220.2 — Lumbar MRI for Low Back Pain

Lumbar MRI is covered for low back pain when ALL of:
1. Documented failure of >=6 weeks of conservative therapy (physical therapy, NSAIDs, activity modification);
2. Persistent symptoms despite conservative care;
3. Plan to alter management based on imaging results.

EXCEPTIONS — the 6-week conservative trial is waived when ANY red-flag indication is present:
(a) New or progressive neurological deficit;
(b) Cauda equina symptoms;
(c) Known or suspected malignancy;
(d) Suspected infection;
(e) Significant trauma.

Acute uncomplicated low back pain (<6 weeks duration) without red flags or completed conservative trial is NOT covered for advanced imaging. Patient pain complaints alone do not establish necessity.

LCD L34960 — Lumbar Fusion Surgery

Lumbar fusion is covered for degenerative disc disease ONLY when ALL of:
1. Documented mechanical instability (translation >4mm, angulation >10 degrees on flexion-extension films), OR high-grade spondylolisthesis, OR confirmed pseudarthrosis from prior fusion;
2. Severe radiculopathy or neurogenic claudication correlating with imaging findings;
3. Documented failure of >=6 months of comprehensive conservative care including physical therapy, medications, and at least one interventional procedure (epidural injection, facet injection).

Disc desiccation or degenerative changes on imaging WITHOUT instability or radiculopathy do NOT meet fusion criteria. 3 months of PT is insufficient conservative care for elective fusion.

Specialty Drug Coverage: Dupilumab (Dupixent) for Atopic Dermatitis

Dupilumab is covered for moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis when documentation establishes:
1. Diagnosis of moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis by a dermatologist;
2. Adequate trial and failure of high-potency topical corticosteroids — 'adequate trial' means continuous use for >=3 months OR documented intolerance/contraindication;
3. Adequate trial and failure of systemic immunosuppressant therapy (cyclosporine, methotrexate, azathioprine, or phototherapy) — again >=3 months continuous use or documented contraindication;
4. Body surface area involvement >=10% OR head/face/genital involvement.

Trial durations of <2-3 weeks do NOT constitute an adequate trial of any prerequisite therapy.
